= product measure and Fubini-Tonelli theorem
<product-measure-and-fubini-tonelli-theorem>
== product space and product measure \[Fol 1.2, finished; 2.5\]
<product-space-and-product-measure-fol-1.2-finished-2.5>
Goal: Given $\(X_i\,cal(A)_i\,mu_i\)$, construct $X = product X_i$, s.t.
$ mu\(E_1 times E_2\)= mu_1\(E_1\)mu_2\(E_2\) $
So that we can do Fubini (iterated integration) like that in Riemann integral.

=== product $sigma$-algebra
<product-sigma-algebra>
#definition(
  title: [#kn[product $sigma$-algebra]],
)[
Suppose $\(X_i\,cal(A)_i\)$ mble, $1 lt.eq i lt.eq n$, the product $sigma$-algebra $A_1 times.o dots.h.c times.o A_n$ on $X_1 times dots.h.c times X_n$ is the smallest #ref[sigma-algebra] s.t. the #strong[coordinate map] $ pi_j : X_1 times dots.h.c times X_n arrow.r X_j $#strong[is measurable.] \ 即 the $sigma$-algebra generated by: ${ pi_alpha\(E_alpha\): E_alpha in cal(A_alpha) }$. $ A_1 times.o dots.h.c times.o A_n : = < { pi_alpha\(E_alpha\): E_alpha in cal(A_alpha) } > $

]
我们容易发现:

#proposition(
)[
$ A_1 times.o dots.h.c times.o A_n = < { E_1 times dots.h.c times E_n in cal(A)_i times dots.h.c times cal(A)_n } > $

]
#proof[
By def 易得. (Prop 1.14 in book). \

]
#remark[
这里只考虑了有限情况, 但是无限的乃至于 ctblly 无限的相似. 取所有可能的 set product 作为 geneating 即可.

]
=== product Borel algebra $subset$ Borel algebra of the product space
<product-borel-algebra-subset-borel-algebra-of-the-product-space>
#proposition(
)[
If $X_1\,dots.h.c\,X_n$ are metric spaces. Let $X := X_1 times dots.h.c times X_n$ (with product metric), then: $ times.o.big_(i = 1)^n cal(B)_(X_i) subset.eq cal(B)_X $
#strong[and the equality holds if $X_i$ separable $forall i$.]

]
#proof[
$ times.o.big_(i = 1)^n cal(B)_(X_i) =^(upright("by prop")) < { U_1 times dots.h.c times U_n upright(" each open") } > subset.eq cal(B)_X $
Now let $C_i subset.eq X_i$ dense, ctbl. \ Set $ cal(E)_i := { B_r\(x\)divides x in C_i #h(0em)\,#h(0em) r in bb(Q)_(> 0) } subset.eq cal(B)_(X_i) $
Then: #strong[every open set in $X_1 times dots.h.c times X_n$ is a ctbl union of products $B_1 times dots.h.c times B_n$], each $B_1 in cal(E)_i$.
Then we have: $ B_X = < { B_1 times . . . times B_n } > subset times.o.big_1^n B_(X_i) $

]
#remark[
显然. #strong[有限 index] 情况下, 在 product topology 中, #strong[product of open sets仍然是 open set], 但是 open sets 可以不止是 product of open sets 这些. 因而 $times.o.big_(i = 1)^n cal(B)_(X_i) subset.eq cal(B)_X$. \ 并且在 separable 的 topological space 上, 比如 $bb(R)$, 我们有: $bb(R)^n$ 中的任意 open set 都是 a ctbl union of open boxes. 于是 $times.o.big_(i = 1)^n cal(B)_(bb(R)) = cal(B)_(bb(R)^n)$

]
#example(
)[
$ cal(B)_(bb(R)^n) = cal(B)_(bb(R)) times.o dots.h.c times.o cal(B)_(bb(R)) $

]
#corollary(
)[
if $\(X\,cal(A)\)$ is a mble space, then $ f : X arrow.r bb(C) #h(0em) #h(0em)\(cal(A)\,cal(B)_(bb(C))\)upright("-mble ") arrow.l.r.double Re f\,Im f #h(0em) #h(0em) cal(A) upright("-mble") $

]
#proof[
略.

]
=== construction of product measure
<construction-of-product-measure>
下面我们构建 product measure:
Let $\(X_i thin\,cal(A)_i thin\,mu_i\)$, $1 lt.eq i lt.eq n$ be mble spaces. \ And let $X := X_1 times . . . times X_n$, $cal(A) := cal(A)_i times.o dots.h.c times.o cal(A)_n$
Goal: 通过 Hahn-Kromolgrov 来构建 product measure on product mble space.
Idea: Let $ cal(A)' := { upright("all finite disjoint unions of rectangles (each measurable)") A_1 times dots.h.c times A_n } $
#strong[Step 1:]

=== all finite disjoint unions of rectangles as an algebra
<all-finite-disjoint-unions-of-rectangles-as-an-algebra>
#proposition(
)[
$cal(A)'$ is an algebra.

]
#proof[
The set $cal(E) := { upright("rectangles") } subset.eq cal(P)\(X\)$ satisfies:

- $diameter in cal(E)$

- $E\,F in cal(E) arrow.r.double.long E inter F in cal(E)$

- $E in cal(E) arrow.r.double.long E^c upright(" is a finite disjoint union of recs")$ (画图可知). \ \

]
#strong[Step 2:]

=== 各维度 measure 的 product 作为 rectangle 的 measure, 从而定义 premeasure
<各维度-measure-的-product-作为-rectangle-的-measure-从而定义-premeasure>
Now define $ mu' : cal(A)' arrow.r\[0\,oo\] $ as follows: $ mu'\(union.sq.big_(k = 1)^N E_1^(\(k\)) times dots.h.c times E_n^(\(k\))\)= sum_(k = 1)^N product_(i = 1)^n mu_i\(E_i^(\(k\))\) $
Claim 2:

#proposition(
)[
#strong[\(1) $mu'$ is a well-defined premeasure on $cal(A)'$. \ (2) If each $mu_i$ is $sigma$-finite, so is $mu'$.]

]
#proof[
Sketch: (2) DIY.
(1) STS(check): if $E = E_1 times dots.h.c E_n$ is a finite or ctbl union of rects $E^(\(k\)) = E_1^(\(k\)) times dots.h.c times E_n^(\(k\))$, then $ product_1^n mu_i\(E_i\)= sum_k product_1^n mu_i\(E_i^(\(k\))\) $
Use Tonelli for sums and integrals: $ product_1^n chi_(E_i)\(x_i\) & = chi_E\(x_1 thin\,dots.h.c thin\,x_n\)\
 & = sum_k chi_(E^(\(k\)))\(x_1 thin\,dots.h.c thin\,x_n\)\
 & = sum_k product_1^n chi_(E_i^(\(k\)))\(x_i\) $
Integrate w.r.t. $x_1$:
$ mu_1\(E_1\)product_(i = 1)^n chi_(E_i)\(x_i\) & = integral sum_k product_1^n chi_(E_i^(\(k\)))\(x_i\)\
 & =^(upright("Tonelli")) sum_k integral\(product_1^n chi_(E_i^(\(k\)))\(x_i\)\)d thin mu_1\(x_1\)\
 & = sum_k mu_1\(E_1^(\(k\))\)product_(i = 1)^n chi_(E_i^(\(k\)))\(x_i\) $
And repeat for $i = 2\,dots.h.c\,n$. \ \

]
=== HK extension of the premeasure as definition of product measure
<hk-extension-of-the-premeasure-as-definition-of-product-measure>
#strong[Step 3: 现在已经有了 $sigma$-finite 的 premeasure, 我们可以应用 HK Thm 构建出完整的 measure.]
Now use HK:

#corollary(
)[
$exists$ measure $mu := mu_1 times dots.h.c times mu_n$ on $cal(A) = cal(A)_1 times.o dots.h.c cal(A)_n$ extending $mu'$. \ (#strong[And if each $mu_i$ are $sigma$-finite, then product measure 也 $sigma$-finite, 从而 $mu$ 是 unique extension.)]

]
由此, 我们从 $cal(A)_1\,dots.h.c\,cal(A)_n$ 的 measure 中构建出了它们的 product measure. \ \

=== associativity of product $sigma$-algebra and $sigma$-finite product measure
<associativity-of-product-sigma-algebra-and-sigma-finite-product-measure>
#corollary(
  title: [#kn[associativity of product measure]],
)[
总有 $ cal(A)_1 times.o cal(A)_2 times.o cal(A)_3 =\(cal(A)_1 times.o cal(A)_2\)times.o cal(A)_3 = cal(A)_1 times.o\(cal(A)_2 times.o cal(A)_3\) $ 并且, if $mu_1\,mu_2\,mu_3$ are $sigma$-finite, then: $ mu_1 times mu_2 times mu_3 =\(mu_1 times mu_2\)times mu_3 = mu_1 times\(mu_2 times mu_3\) $

]
#proof[
DIY. 前者 play with def, 后者直接由 $sigma$-finite 的 premeasure 的 HK extension unique 得到.

]
=== 如何证明一个函数 product measurable
<如何证明一个函数-product-measurable>
要证明一个函数是 product measurable 的, 只需要证明它对于每个 measurable rectangle 的 preimage 都是 measurable 的即可.

#lemma(
)[
Suppose $f : X arrow.r Y times Z$ is a function from a measurable space $\(X\,cal(A)\)$ to a product measure space $\(Y times Z\,cal(B)_1 times.o cal(B)_2\)$. \ Claim: If $f^(- 1)\(B_1 times B_2\)in cal(A)$ for each measurable rectangle $B_1 times B_2 in cal(B)_1 times.o cal(B)_2$, then $f$ is an $\(cal(A)\,cal(B)_1 times.o cal(B)_2\)$-measurable function.

]
#proof[
因为 product $sigma$-algebra 由所有的 measurable rectangles 生成. \ Hw7 中有另一版的证明作为 lemma.

]
在 Hw7 中我们可以通过这个 lemma 得到一个结论: 如果 $E in cal(A times.o A)$, 那么 $E$ 的 diagonal 一定 $in cal(A)$.

对于特殊的函数, 比如两个 measurable function 的乘积, 其一定是 product measurable 的.

#lemma(
  title: [#kn[easier Fubini]],
)[
条件: $\(X\,cal(A)\,mu\)$, $\(Y\,cal(B)\,nu\)$ 为 arbitrary measure space (不需要 $sigma$-finite.), $f : X arrow.r bb(C)$, $g : Y arrow.r bb(C)$ 为 measurable functions. \ 结论: $ h := f g quad upright("is ")\(cal(A) times.o cal(B)\)upright("-measurable") $
并且如果 $f\,g$ 是 $L^1$ 的, 那么 $h in L^1\(mu times nu\)$ 并且 $ integral h #h(0em) d\(mu times nu\)= \( integral f #h(0em) d mu \) \( integral g #h(0em) d nu \) $

]
#proof[
in hw 8. 这个 statement 表示一个 $cal(A) upright("-measurable")$ 的函数和一个 $cal(B) upright("-measurable")$ 的函数的乘积是 $\(cal(A) times.o cal(B)\)upright("-measurable")$ 的.

]
